anaged:"The resident instance serves v{served} but has **no watchdog keeping it alive** (an orphan left by a stop or a hard kill) \u2014 use the button below to put it back under management (a fresh watchdog plus a new instance), or run {cmd}",vcResidentLockUnknownShort:"management unknown",vcResidentReplaceBlockedShort:"cannot replace",vcResidentHostManagedShort:"host-managed",vcResidentReplaceBlocked:'The resident instance **cannot be replaced** (environment limit): the watchdog lock directory is not writable ({err}; {path}) \u2192 the port will stay on v{served} **long-term**. This is not "temporarily behind": automatic replacement is refused on purpose to avoid leaving an orphan. Way out: fix that directory permissions and run {cmd}, or run dsh-memory watchdog --port 7999 in the foreground',vcResidentLockUnknown:'The resident instance serves v{served}, but the **watchdog lock file cannot be written** (restricted environment: sandbox, ACLs, non-system drive) \u2192 whether it is managed cannot be determined (this is not "unmanaged"). Cause: {err} ({path}). Keep-alive usually still works; the button below can put it back under management on the new code.',vcPage:"Page script",vcPageStale:"\u26A0 This page is still running an older script (page v{page} / disk v{disk}): press Ctrl+F5 to refresh. If the running version is still old, restart the desktop app / DSH as well",vcOutdated:"update available",vcUpToDate:"up to date",vcCheck:"Check for updates",checking:"Checking\u2026",vcCheckFail:"Update check failed",recallSummaryLen:"Recall summary len",recallBody:"Recall with body",secretHint:"Credential hint (injected into every session)",autoWeb:"Web server",autoWebMode:"Keep-alive mode",webPort:"Web port",webCheckIntervalMs:"Probe interval (ms)",webMaxRestart:"Max restart",watchdogAutoSpawn:"Watchdog process",autoRestartOnDrift:"Auto-restart resident on version drift",autoMcpSetup:"Auto-mount MCP",saveConfig:"Save config",saveFail:"Save failed",savedOk:"Saved",savedDir